WEBVTT

00:25:56.947 --> 00:26:00.006
that if you really encourage
the dreamy version of their career,

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:01.835
it actually looks quite bold.

00:26:01.859 --> 00:26:03.573
And then once you know what it is,

00:26:03.597 --> 00:26:06.960
then you can kind of together
be plotting with them,

00:26:06.984 --> 00:26:08.808
"Well, how can you get from A to B?"

00:26:08.832 --> 00:26:11.971
And how can you help them
draw on the strengths they already have,

00:26:11.995 --> 00:26:15.214
and where are the places that they can,
little by little by little,

00:26:15.238 --> 00:26:16.782
step outside their comfort zone?

00:26:16.806 --> 00:26:21.552
CA: Well, so, talk more about
the introvert-extrovert issue at work,

00:26:21.576 --> 00:26:24.955
because you've got
fairly passionately held opinions

00:26:24.979 --> 00:26:31.887
on how work offices, for example,
could and should be organized.